---
/** Section 6: walk back from a line of code to the goal; links can be broken. */
---

<div class="audit-walk not-content">
	<div class="audit-walk__controls">
		<button type="button" class="sdlc-btn sdlc-btn--primary" data-walk="back">↑ Why is this here?</button>
		<button type="button" class="sdlc-btn" data-walk="reset">Start again</button>
		<span class="audit-walk__count" aria-live="polite"></span>
	</div>
	<div class="audit-walk__breaks">
		<span class="sdlc-legend__hint">Break a link:</span>
		<label><input type="checkbox" data-break="no-refs" /> commit message "update", no <code>Refs:</code></label>
		<label><input type="checkbox" data-break="chat-only" /> plan answers given only in chat</label>
		<label><input type="checkbox" data-break="no-adr" /> no decision record</label>
	</div>
	<ol class="audit-walk__steps">
		<li class="audit-walk__step"><b>Line of code</b><span class="audit-walk__how"><code>lib/config.dart</code>, line 14</span><span class="audit-walk__code">const appVersion = String.fromEnvironment('APP_VERSION', defaultValue: 'dev');</span><span class="audit-walk__q">"Every tutorial uses package_info_plus to read the version. Why don't we? Can I add it?"</span></li>
		<li class="audit-walk__step" data-needs="no-refs"><b>Commit</b><span class="audit-walk__how">found with <code>git blame -L 14,14 lib/config.dart</code></span><span class="audit-walk__code">3f2a9c1 feat(app): add About screen with app and server version
Refs: GOAL-1 · ADR: ADR-0003 · AI-assisted: GitHub Copilot (agent)</span></li>
		<li class="audit-walk__step"><b>Pull request #12</b><span class="audit-walk__how">found with <code>gh pr list --state merged --search "GOAL-1"</code></span><span>Reviewed and approved by another pair. The description links the plan and lists <code>docs/adr/0003-app-version-from-build.md</code> under Documentation.</span></li>
		<li class="audit-walk__step" data-needs="chat-only"><b>Plan</b><span class="audit-walk__how">linked from the pull request</span><span class="audit-walk__code">Q2  Version: package_info_plus or --dart-define?
A2  --dart-define, as in ADR-0002. No new package.
    Record it as an ADR.   (answered by the pair, 2026-11-19)</span></li>
		<li class="audit-walk__step" data-needs="no-adr"><b>Decision record: ADR-0003</b><span class="audit-walk__how">the plan points to it</span><span><em>Context:</em> every package is a SOUP item (IEC 62304): it needs a row in <code>docs/soup.csv</code>, an assessment and updates for as long as the app lives. <em>Decision:</em> the build passes the version with <code>--dart-define</code>. <em>Consequence:</em> debug builds show "dev"; if we need more platform information, revisit this with a new ADR.</span></li>
		<li class="audit-walk__step"><b>Acceptance criterion AC-2</b><span class="audit-walk__how">the plan maps its steps to criteria</span><span>"The screen shows the app version and build number of the build, for example <code>1.3.0 (12)</code>…"</span></li>
		<li class="audit-walk__step"><b>Goal: GOAL-1</b><span class="audit-walk__how">named at the top of <code>docs/spec-about.md</code></span><span>About screen, from issue #7: "Support can tell which version a participant runs."</span></li>
		<li class="audit-walk__end"><b>Trail complete</b>No package is a recorded decision with a reason, not an oversight. To change it, write a new ADR that supersedes ADR-0003, add the SOUP row, and the trail continues.</li>
		<li class="audit-walk__break" data-break="no-refs"><b>Trail lost at the commit</b>The message says "update" and names no goal. Which feature was this for? You can only guess from the date, and searching for the goal will not find this commit.</li>
		<li class="audit-walk__break" data-break="chat-only"><b>Trail lost at the plan</b>The question "package or <code>--dart-define</code>?" was answered in a chat that no longer exists. Was it a decision or a guess? Nobody can tell, so somebody will "fix" it.</li>
		<li class="audit-walk__break" data-break="no-adr"><b>Trail lost at the decision</b>The plan says "no new package", but there is no decision record to point to. Decided by whom, and why? Without it the reason is gone, and the next agent session adds <code>package_info_plus</code>, because that is what most code on the internet does.</li>
	</ol>
</div>

<script>
	import '../scripts/sdlc.js';
</script>
